<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd">

    <!--
        ORG-WIDE REBRAND FOLLOW-UP for the module registration seeds 022/023/024/025/
        028/029/031/033 — repoint every remaining remote_entry_url from a sibling UI's
        pre-rebrand k8s Service short-name to its rebranded hugmesh-* one. This is the
        same-mechanism generalisation of 039 (which did exactly this for
        character-forge); see 039's header for the full rationale. In short:

          - The registration changesets are MERGED history and may already have run in
            live databases: editing their seed values in place would break their
            Liquibase checksums (ValidationFailedException on startup) AND would not
            migrate rows in already-migrated DBs (a RAN changeSet never re-executes).
            Only NEW additive UPDATEs can do both. The historical files are therefore
            left byte-for-byte as shipped.

          - Each changeSet below is guarded (preCondition MARK_RAN + the same predicate
            repeated in the <where>) on the EXACT pre-rebrand URL, so it is idempotent
            and never clobbers an operator/superadmin override of remote_entry_url
            (the admin control plane can rewrite this column). updated_at is bumped to
            mirror what ModuleRegistryService/AdminModuleService do on any row
            mutation. Each rollback restores the pre-rebrand URL. The pre-rebrand
            spellings below exist ONLY as match predicates for rows seeded by the
            immutable historical changesets — they are the migration away from those
            names, not usage of them.

          - DEPLOY ORDERING (same caveat as 039): each value must match the sibling's
            actual k8s Service name after the generator's manifest rename wave
            (specs/cluster/manifests/**). This changelog must not reach a cluster
            before those manifest renames do, or a remote entry would resolve to a
            Service that does not exist yet.

          - NOT RENAMED HERE (frozen, per reserved-prefixes.yaml + the merged
            registrations): the FEATURE SLUGS themselves (forum, mastodon, matrix,
            games, wiki, mod, apidocs, user, owncast, tube), their metadata.mountAt
            values, and the gateway route prefixes. Only the BRAND PREFIX on each
            sibling service's hostname changes.
    -->

    <changeSet id="041-1-rebrand-forum-remote-entry" author="federation">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="1">
                SELECT COUNT(*) FROM federation_modules
                 WHERE slug = 'forum'
                   AND remote_entry_url = 'http://snapdragon-forum-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json'
            </sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>
        <update tableName="federation_modules">
            <column name="remote_entry_url" value="http://hugmesh-forum-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json"/>
            <column name="updated_at" valueComputed="${now}"/>
            <where>
                slug = 'forum'
                AND remote_entry_url = 'http://snapdragon-forum-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json'
            </where>
        </update>
        <rollback>
            <update tableName="federation_modules">
                <column name="remote_entry_url" value="http://snapdragon-forum-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json"/>
                <column name="updated_at" valueComputed="${now}"/>
                <where>
                    slug = 'forum'
                    AND remote_entry_url = 'http://hugmesh-forum-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json'
                </where>
            </update>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

